ul-mccartney-jane-asher_001-768x585.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_paul-mccartney-jane-asher_001.jpg 849w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"8524\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/68_paul-mccartney-jane-asher_001/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_paul-mccartney-jane-asher_001.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"849,647\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"4\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney and Jane Asher, 1968\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_paul-mccartney-jane-asher_001.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>She was the youngest of three children born to Dr Richard Alan John Asher and Margaret Asher. Her father worked as a writer, broadcaster and consultant in blood and mental diseases at Central Middlesex Hospital, and her mother was a professor of oboe at the Guildhall School of Music and Drama.</p><p>Asher became a child actress and later had a distinguished career on stage and screen.</p>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 26 May 2020</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2025: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2025/04/05/pete-best-announces-retirement/\">Pete Best announces retirement</a></li><li>2019: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2019/04/05/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-tokyo-dome-city-hall-tokyo/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Tokyo Dome City Hall, Tokyo</a></li><li>2017: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2017/04/05/beatles-sgt-pepper-50th-anniversary-edition/\">Full details of The Beatles’ Sgt Pepper 50th anniversary edition</a></li><li>2010: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2010/04/05/paul-mccartney-live-coliseo-de-puerto-rico-san-juan/\">Paul McCartney live: Coliseo de Puerto Rico, 